   102	* 11 check markers in prose match 11 entries in `checks/claims/02.tsv`.
   103	* Aside from the misplaced `02-cra-roles` marker and the 2024 vs 2025 survey date discrepancy, citations accurately reflect the underlying primary legislation, vendor pages, and research papers.
   104	
   105	### 9. Verdict and Kill Assumption
   106	* **Verdict:** `TEST THROUGH A PARTNER` (Correct; direct selling is barred by language/trust, making channel viability the gating dependency).
   107	* **Kill Assumption:** *"The assumption most able to reverse it is that an enabled partner will keep buying recurring specialist capacity instead of internalising the routine work and retaining the full margin."* (Accurately identifies the central existential vulnerability).
   108	
   109	### 10. Readability
   110	* Paragraph lengths are well balanced (all between 40 and 100 words).
   111	* Jargon (SBOM, CRA, PSIRT, IEC 62443) is grounded in specific operational mechanisms.
   112	* 3 sentences exceed 40 words and need minor splitting.
   113	
